{"availability":"available","full":"zjoooooo/galaxy-explorer","name":"galaxy-explorer","description":"🌌 An interactive, procedurally-generated Milky Way galaxy in the browser — WebGL / three.js, no backend, no build step. MIT licensed.","category":"Design","language":"HTML","stars":97,"forks":8,"created":"2026-07-04T03:03:32Z","updated":"2026-10-15T13:59:25Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://zjoooooo.github.io/galaxy-explorer/","topics":["astronomy","creative-coding","galaxy","generative-art","procedural-generation","shaders","space","threejs","visualization","webgl"],"demo":"https://zjoooooo.github.io/galaxy-explorer/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:15.311Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:15.311Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:15.311Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:00:04.342Z","stars":96,"forks":8},{"at":"2026-10-12T13:38:04.957Z","stars":97,"forks":8},{"at":"2026-10-15T15:01:15.311Z","stars":97,"forks":8}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An interactive, procedurally-generated Milky Way galaxy — with a full 3D Solar System, a roaming comet, and real radio-galaxy jets — that runs entirely in the browser with WebGL (three.js). No backend, no build step, no dependencies to install, no API keys — just open the page and explore.","The galaxy itself is generated in code at load time: almost no image assets — the spiral arms, nebula gas, star clusters, distant galaxies and supernovae are all math (the Magellanic Clouds and Centaurus A additionally sample their star positions and colours from three CC BY photo plates). The Solar System layers real NASA-based surface textures on top for the planets, moons and Sun.","Free for any use — personal, commercial, academic and teaching — under the MIT License."],"features":["Spiral disc — 85,000 dust points on four density-wave arms, with a warm","core fading to cool blue arms, bright star knots, HII regions and blu